# The local internal repository (file:///var/lib/droidian-internal-repository)
# holds this port's patched packages.
#
# The Droidian rolling repository is pinned at priority 1002. Whenever a
# competing package (phosh, for example) exists there at a higher version, apt
# picks THAT one and our patched .deb never reaches the image - the "apt/ trap".
# A version bump is not enough to win.
#
# Pinning the internal repository at 1100 (> 1002, and > 1000, which also allows
# a forced downgrade) makes it win unconditionally.
#
# An empty "origin" matches a local file:// repository.
Package: *
Pin: origin ""
Pin-Priority: 1100
